{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The multimodal setup with pca_n2000 + resnet50 (config_016, acc=0.527) outperforms RNA-only (config_001, acc=0.485) by ~4%, and concat fusion marginally beats weighted (0.527 vs 0.523). Image-only is very weak (0.208), confirming the image modality contributes little standalone but may add complementary signal in fusion. The major untested dimension is profile_setting: all completed experiments used singleprofile, so we have no evidence on whether aggregating multiple profiles per cell improves representations. Question tested: Does multiprofile aggregation (via avgpool) on top of the current best multimodal pipeline (pca_n2000 + resnet50 + concat) yield a meaningful accuracy gain over the singleprofile baseline? Why this is the best next experiment: It is the most logical exploitation of the strongest-performing direction while simultaneously resolving the largest remaining uncertainty (profile setting). Using avgpool keeps the aggregation simple and low-risk, and concat is retained as the slightly preferred fusion from prior evidence. If multiprofile helps, it opens a high-value axis for further refinement (e.g., transformer aggregation, different encoders); if it does not, we efficiently rule out an entire block of 20+ multiprofile configurations, saving budget for RNA-encoder exploration."
}

